    "event": "Flood Warning",
    "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
    "senderName": "NWS Phoenix AZ",
    "headline": "Flood Warning issued October 31 at 6:07AM MST until October 31 at 12:15PM MST by NWS Phoenix AZ",
    "description": "* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues.\n\n* WHERE...Gila County in east central Arizona...\n\n* WHEN...Until 1215 PM MST Saturday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of Tonto Creek and flood-prone locations is\nimminent or occurring. Tonto Creek continues to rise due to excess\nrunoff from earlier rainfall. Low-water crossings are inundated\nwith water and may not be passable.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 607 AM MST, a streamflow gauge on Tonto Creek north of Tonto\nBasin rose above action stage, with a stage height of 5.12 feet\nand flow of 2422 cfs as of 515 AM MST. Flooding is ongoing or\nexpected to begin shortly along Tonto Creek in the warned area.\nPlease use the Tonto Creek Bridge for all travel across the\ncreek. Bar X Crossing, and any other low water crossings, will\nlikely become impassable.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nTonto Basin.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
    "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nBe aware of your surroundings and do not drive on flooded roads.",
    "response": "Avoid",
    "note": null,
